Hungarian playwright Ferenc Molnár was almost never awake until afternoon. Once when he was forced to get up early in the morning because of jury duty, he looked unbelievingly at the people crowding the Budapest streets and asked, &#8216;Are they <em>all</em> jurors?&#8217;
</p></blockquote>
<p>&#8212; Shirley Motter Linde, <em>The Sleep Book</em>, 1974</p>
